        "id": 2699564073,
        "content": "It is fine to use rounding in this code because this only has display purposes, however the root of the problem is not the rounding itself but JS having problems with floating points operations, because the current code:\n`result: Object.values(formatting).reduce((acc, curr) => acc + curr.score * curr.elementCount, 0)`\nShould never yield results with infinite decimal points like we've seen. A proposer fix is to use the Decimal library like we do in the rest of the codebase.",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity-os-marketplace/text-conversation-rewards/issues/292#issuecomment-2699564073",
        "commentType": "ISSUE_AUTHOR",
        "score": {
